      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the value of the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we can recognize that this expression is in the form of a perfect square trinomial. The binomial expansion of \\((a + b)^2\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nIn our case, we can identify \\(a = 23\\) and \\(b = 2\\). Substituting these values into the binomial expansion formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = (23 + 2)^2\n\\]\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n23 + 2 = 25\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(23 + 2)^2 = 25^2\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(25^2\\):\n\n\\[\n25^2 = 25 \\times 25 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{625}\\).",
